    {
      id: 'yoruba-6', title: '奥巴塔拉在泥土前许诺', tag: '约鲁巴塑人与关怀',
      summary: '奥巴塔拉用泥土塑造人的身体，饮下棕榈酒后却失去专注。他醒来面对已经完成的身体，立誓戒酒并承担保护责任，生命仍由至高者赋予。',
      paragraphs: [
        '约鲁巴关于造人的一支叙事说，奥巴塔拉负责以泥土塑造身体，至高者奥洛杜马雷则赋予生命。他坐在泥土前，逐一制作人的形体；塑成身体与使身体活起来，是彼此关联却并不相同的职责，不能全归于同一个行动。',
        '工作期间，奥巴塔拉饮下棕榈酒，醉意使他不再像原先那样专注。他继续塑形，做出身体各有不同的人。等酒醒后，他看见自己已经完成的工作，因未能谨慎履职而自责；事情不能靠把泥重新揉合，就当作从来没有发生。',
        '奥巴塔拉于是立誓不再饮酒，并承担对不同身体者的特别保护。这属于一支宗教起源叙事，不是身体差异的医学解释，更不表示任何人有罪或价值较低。故事最后落在照料责任，而非允许人以神话作为排斥他人的理由。'
      ],
      en: {
        title: 'Obatala Makes a Promise beside the Clay', tag: 'Yoruba creation and care',
        summary: 'Obatala shapes human bodies from clay but loses concentration after drinking palm wine. Confronting his completed work, he promises abstinence and particular protection, while the giving of life remains the responsibility of the supreme deity.',
        paragraphs: [
          'In one Yoruba account of human origins, Obatala shapes bodies from clay, while the supreme deity, Olodumare, gives them life. Working with the earth before him, he forms human figures individually. Making a body and making that body live are connected responsibilities, but the narrative does not assign them to exactly the same action.',
          'During his work, Obatala drinks palm wine and becomes intoxicated. His concentration changes, yet he continues molding, producing people with differing bodies. When he becomes sober, he confronts what he has already made and regrets his lack of care. These completed human forms cannot simply be kneaded away as though nothing has happened.',
          'Obatala promises to abstain from wine and undertakes particular protection of people with bodily differences. This religious origin narrative is not a medical explanation of disability, nor does it make anyone blameworthy or less valuable. Its conclusion concerns responsibility and care; it cannot justify using sacred tradition as permission to exclude other people.'
        ]
      }
    }
